  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1216 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nSurface high pressure centered over the Midwest today will maintain \ncontrol of our weather through mid week as it gradually shifts east \ntowards the Appalachians through Wednesday. Southerly winds return \nstarting Tuesday which allows temperatures to return to above normal \nreadings in the 60s by mid week. In the upper levels, ridging builds \nacross the Ohio Valley heading into mid week. Meanwhile, shortwave \nenergy ejects out of the Rockies and pivots into the Upper Midwest \non Wednesday. This system stays well northwest of our area though, \nwith ridging remaining in place through late week. Additional \nshortwave energy ejects across the central CONUS heading into next \nweekend which may allow a cold frontal passage and associated \nprecipitation to impact our region by Saturday or Saturday night.\n\nNBM guidance continues to indicate a high probability of \ntemperatures reaching 70 degrees late in the week, peaking around 70-\n80% on Saturday. Glancing out further, there is a signal for a \ncooler pattern to return for the week of Thanksgiving (Nov 23-27) \nwith an increased probability for temperatures returning to below \nnormal levels.",
